[deps
  [doc [#
The repositories `cx` builds on, each at a sha (RULED: RS-7).

THE FORMAT is spec/03-approved/process/repository-dependency-pins.md. One [dep]
row per pinned REPOSITORY -- not per module. `sha` is the pin; `tag` records
the release it was taken from; `v-fork` is carried by a V repository's row.
`cx scripts/deps_sync.cx` reads this document, fetches each pin shallowly into
an ignored deps/<repo>/, and FAILS on a stale pin or a drifted checkout. It
never warns (#1591; #1589 "Risks": the previous stale-copy arrangement rotted
within weeks because nothing failed when it did).

A ROW IS TAKEN WHEN THE REPOSITORY EXISTS AND HAS RELEASED, not before. There
is no placeholder row and the format forbids one: Sec 2 makes `sha` required and
40 lowercase hexadecimal characters, and refuses any key it does not list, so
`sha=none` is `malformed-sha` and `status=not-yet-extracted` is `unknown-key`.
That is the right refusal -- a pin that cannot be fetched is not a pin -- and
it means THIS DOCUMENT IS NOT THE ROSTER OF THE SHAPE. The roster is
registry/repos.cxd, which carries all twenty-eight [repo] rows including `cx`'s
own; `make repos-allocation-gate` joins the two and prints how many of the
twenty-seven other repositories are pinned today. A repository in the roster
with no row here has not been extracted yet, and `cx` is still the whole tree
for it.

TODAY: one row. `cx-platform-sso` is the first extraction (#1591 item 11,
RS-12's "quietest first") and the only repository of the shape that exists on
GitHub. Its module's source has not left this tree yet, so
`make bundle-compose` reports it `migrating` -- pinned, and embedded from the
tracked copy until the extraction commit deletes it. The other twenty-six rows
land with their extractions, in RS-12's order:

  cx-core-data  cx-core-code
  cx-platform-{net, mail, identity, store, db, fabric, xap}
  cx-platform-{flow, connector, ux, agent}
  cx-binding-{python, go, rust, v}
  cx-binding-{typescript, java, kotlin, csharp, swift, ruby}   (archived)
  cx-registry  cx-decisions  cx-tooling

WHAT A PIN BUYS THE BUILD. `scripts/deps_sync.cx --vpath` turns the rows
carrying a `v-fork` into V's `-path` value, and `scripts/bundle_compose.cx`
turns the rest into the bundled CX sources the four `cx` builds embed --
`make deps-sync && make build-vcx` is the whole story, and a pinned repository
whose deps/ checkout is missing FAILS the build by name rather than producing a
smaller binary (conformance/bundle_sources.cxd, case bundle-010).

`cx` is a migration lane, never a gate (RS-7): when any repository releases,
`cx` tries the newest mutually green set; green advances the pins, red leaves
them and the finding lands on the repository that moved. No merge anywhere
waits on `cx`. A release cut ships whatever is pinned.
#]]

  [dep repo=cx-platform-sso sha=d1b9d2bcca52c5ec7c66cd4a958d5a729cc7eddd module='cx-platform/sso']
]
